  Just for fun, I wanted to play around with a wand of polymorph
and piles o' stuff, but I was too lazy to sit and cycle through the
characters needed to get me one.  So I pulled out "expect" (a neat
utility from don libes, available wherever archie says it's at) and
wrote this little cheat thing.  It keeps rolling up wizards until
I get my wand, or whatever else you put in there (right now this
looks for wands of poly and death as well as +3 items.)

 -- d

(Comments and caveats -- you can ^C this, and when it dies, it
should have saved the character currently being rolled, so you
can start up hack again and it will restore it.  This is handy if
you're watching this thing work and it flashes up stormbringer or
something in the inventory and you didn't think of putting it
in as a clause.  Also, ^Z'ing out of a game will nuke the game --
expect does odd things.  Anyway... run out and get expect.  Neat
tool to have around, in any case (works on most unix systems, not
on MS-DOS, I think)).

#!/usr/local/bin/expect -f
#
#  keep rolling wizards until you get an item with the word "death"
# (aka wand of death), "+3", or "wand of polymorph" in it.
#

set timeout 2
for {} 1 {} {
	spawn /usr/games/nethack

	expect { *Shall* }	{ send "n" }
	expect { *Wizard* }	{ send "w" }
	expect { *--More--* }	{ send " " }
	expect { *welcome* }	{ send "i" }
	expect  { *death* *+3* *wand\ of\ polym*} { send " " ; break } \
		timeout				{ send " " }

	expect { * }		{ send "Q" }
	expect { *quit* }	{ send "y" }
	expect { *identifi* }	{ send "n" }
	expect { *intrinsi* }	{ send "n" }
	expect { *More* }	{ send " " }

	wait
	close
	}
interact


